- Story & Context: On the rooftop observatory of Ostraca during the first deep-freeze of the dune-winter, bandleader Zaza tried to align a brass brass-mounted telescope with Jupiter, only for the lens to snap violently from the rapid temperature drop while an old synth hummed in the engine room below. The shock of the cracking glass caused the caravan's youth to burst into an impromptu, manic dance, drumming on the metal chassis with spanners until sunrise. This track captures that violent, joyful freezing point, combining hyper-speed mandolin picking with a booming post-punk bassline. Over the sonic chaos, Zaza screams the iconic opening line: "Blow the shattered dust from the glass, tonight we measure heaven in shards!"
