- Story & Context: Legend has it that during the historic power outage of the Great Salt Drift, the entire caravan went pitch black mid-chorus, leaving fifty thousand dancers stranded in darkness on the dunes. Instead of stopping, the Zenith Scavengers kept playing acoustically, cranking their mandolins frantically while the crowd sang the chord progressions in four-part harmony under an unclouded view of the Milky Way. When the dynamos flickered back to life, the synths roared with a strange, pitch-shifted resonance that sounded like the stars themselves humming. This track stands as the mythic climax of the EP, capturing that legendary moment of unyielding, communal euphoria with the echoed vocal hook: "Darkness only means the sky gets to play the lead vocal."
